- **Founding** one needs two or more Awakened, each paying the 3 Karma.
  Once a month they roll to establish a link, against TN 12 with modifiers;
  extra dice cost 3 Karma each *(MitS p.65)*.

{: .note }
> Building initiation, metamagic and the other *Magic in the Shadows* Karma
> costs into the system is planned (TODO 219).

Four Intelligence-linked skills cover the Matrix: **Computer** (legitimate use — logons, moving
around, ordinary prompts; defaults from Electronics), **Hacking** (illegal or scrutinized action,
opposed by the target's Sys/Sec; defaults from Computer), **Cybercombat** (fighting other icons;
defaults from Computer), and **Programming** (writing or fixing utilities, skillsofts and agents;
defaults from Computer).

{: .note }
> The system doesn't track subscriber lists or affiliation: the GM keeps
> count of how many drones the deck is controlling.

Vehicle armor is **hardened**: a hit whose Power (after the vehicle-mass
halving below) doesn't exceed the Armor Rating does nothing at all;
otherwise Armor reduces Power like ordinary armor.

- **Revolvers** can't take silencers or sound suppressors; **hold-outs**
  take no accessories. **SMGs** take sound suppressors but not silencers;
  **shotguns** take neither.

{: .house }
> **Optional flavor, not from the books.** Tracking tags or corporate lockouts
> on stolen high-end implants, and a time limit for pulling chrome from a
> corpse, are good complications. If you use them, set the tests yourself;
> neither book gives numbers.
